Checkpoint 11 owner validation - Skaping ingestion
===================================================

Historical validation notice: polling and outbox details below were
superseded by `validation_first_code_review_after_step12`.

Status: ready for owner validation.

1. Automated tests
------------------

    uv run --env-file .env pytest -q \
      tests/ingestion/skaping tests/ingestion/windy \
      tests/ingestion/fintraffic tests/ingestion/shared \
      tests/metrics tests/storage tests/notification

Confirm ETag extraction, body-free followed HEAD, `Last-Modified` conversion,
HEAD/GET race rejection, image limits, shared transformation/publication, and
provider regressions pass.

Run the real registry scheduling tests:

    RUN_DATABASE_TESTS=1 uv run --env-file .env pytest -q \
      tests/database/test_registry_queries.py

Confirm the default provider-marker policy still passes its Windy/Fintraffic
tests, while only `adaptive_polling_anchor="download_timestamp"` applies the
Skaping download-time and freshness-attempt guards.

2. Bounded read-only provider check
-----------------------------------

    just ingest-skaping --limit 10 --dry-run

Confirm at most ten active `ska` streams are selected. Changed streams may be
downloaded and validated in memory, but no database, S3, or MQTT write occurs.
Provider markers must be ETags; do not expect a timestamp-shaped marker.

3. Bounded complete pipeline
----------------------------

    just infrastructure
    just ingest-skaping --limit 4 --publish

Confirm changed images report `published`, an S3 object key under
`T0V0/ska/`, and an MQTT topic. In PostgreSQL, inspect without printing full
provider metadata:

    docker compose exec postgres psql \
      -U webcam_ingestion -d webcam_ingestion -P pager=off -c \
      "SELECT source_stream_id, last_provider_image_marker,
              last_download_timestamp, estimated_source_stream_period
       FROM source_stream ss JOIN site s USING (site_id)
       WHERE s.network_id='ska'
       ORDER BY last_download_timestamp DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10;"

After a failed HEAD or download, verify the same stream is not selected again
until at least 300 seconds after `last_freshness_query_timestamp`. An unchanged
successful stream is governed by both that freshness-query guard and
`last_download_timestamp + max(300 seconds, 0.7 * estimated_source_stream_period)`.

4. Monitored worker
-------------------

    just ingestion-test-skaping 20m staggered

The recipe prints its screen session and log. Confirm Prometheus target
`skaping-worker-host-benchmark` is up on port 8015 and open the provisioned
`Skaping ingestion worker` dashboard through the existing Grafana tunnel.
Confirm all displayed worker queries are filtered to `source_network="ska"`.

Check provider refresh and download outcomes, job and five-minute throughput,
source/derived metadata percentiles, external/S3 MB/s, provider-to-download
latency, transformation, S3, MQTT, and controlled failures. `Last-Modified`
represents provider storage availability, not guaranteed capture time.

5. Acceptance
-------------

Review:

    git diff --check
    git status --short

Accept checkpoint 11 only after the bounded publication and provider-filtered
dashboard behave as described.
